// Named value in an API Management gateway
//
// A value policies refer to by name, selected by `name`. The value itself
// is deliberately not exposed. What matters for an audit is `secret`,
// which says whether the value is stored encrypted, and `keyVault`, which
// says whether it is held in Key Vault rather than in the gateway
// configuration: a secret kept inline is readable by anyone who can read
// the service configuration and is not rotated with the rest of the
// estate.
